24744564294815,0.0,0.0,-0.00024530262453481555,-0.6988976001739502,-0.2712797224521637,-2.3841855067985307e-07,-2.3841855067985307e-07,0.0,0.0,-2.5033637939486653e-05,-5.125986263010418e-06,-2.861018856492592e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,23606,400,87,61,18,488,220,23,87,61,17,481,220,19,87,488,272,284,220,15,3,702,2326,19703,11,825,315,892,374,279,2629,315,279,1008,1378,13,3555,374,400,66,3,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe equation $x^3 + 8x^2 - 4x + c = 0$ has three roots, one of which is the sum of the other two. What is $c$?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"5fa7534e02f7c900a7d7aa202cd86fe95cdaf3f22d49c50bc89ae26e00dd4268"},"seconds":28.58747363090515,"seed":398063274345382330,"stop":"eos","text":"Let the roots of the cubic equation $x^3 + 8x^2 - 4x + c = 0$ be $\\alpha$, $\\beta$, and $\\gamma$, where $\\gamma = \\alpha + \\beta$. Using Vieta's formulas, we can relate the roots to the coefficients of the polynomial as follows:\n\n1. The sum of the roots taken one at a time is $\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = -\\frac{8}{1} = -8$.\n2. The sum of the products of the roots taken two at a time is $\\alpha\\beta + \\beta\\gamma + \\gamma\\alpha = \\frac{-4}{1} = -4$.\n3. The product of the roots is $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = -c$.\n\nGiven that $\\gamma = \\alpha + \\beta$, we substitute $\\gamma$ in the equations:\n\n1. $\\alpha + \\beta + (\\alpha + \\beta) = -8 \\Rightarrow 2(\\alpha + \\beta) = -8 \\Rightarrow \\alpha + \\beta = -4$.\n2. We substitute $\\gamma = \\alpha + \\beta = -4$ into the second equation:\n   \\[\n   \\alpha\\beta + \\beta(\\alpha + \\beta) + \\alpha(\\alpha + \\beta) = -4 \\Rightarrow \\alpha\\beta + \\beta(-4) + \\alpha(-4) = -4 \\Rightarrow \\alpha\\beta - 4(\\alpha + \\beta) = -4\n   \\]\n   Since $\\alpha + \\beta = -4$, we have:\n   \\[\n   \\alpha\\beta - 4(-4) = -4 \\Rightarrow \\alpha\\beta + 16 = -4 \\Rightarrow \\alpha\\beta = -20\n   \\]\n\n3. For the product of the roots $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma = -c$, we substitute $\\gamma = -4$ and $\\alpha\\beta = -20$:\n   \\[\n   (-20)(-4) = -c \\Rightarrow 80 = -c \\Rightarrow c = -80\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of $c$ is \\(\\boxed{-80}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{-80}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
